    "body": "## DOC: Fix the reverse description of winblend on mini.map\r\n\r\n### 0 makes it transparent:\r\n![0](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45848083/215269761-b05931d3-7c8a-4091-ad33-aadd255a181a.png)\r\n\r\n### 100 makes it opaque:\r\n![100](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45848083/215269777-6c1260b2-1abd-4d52-b0e5-704973703bc1.png)\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-01-28T14:32:33Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ## DOC: Fix the reverse description of winblend on mini.map\r\n> ### 0 makes it transparent:\r\n> \r\n> ### 100 makes it opaque:\r\n> \r\n>     * [x]  I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n> \r\n>     * [x]  I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nThanks for PR!\r\n\r\nHowever, the current documentation is correct. Documentation is taken almost verbatim [from corresponding 'winblend' option](https://neovim.io/doc/user/options.html#'winblend'). And [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/81a575e0c51d4607bf6690f12906c7590d961717/lua/mini/map.lua#L1389-L1390) where it is used directly.\r\n\r\nHere is my experience with `winblend = 0`:\r\n\r\n![map_winblend-0](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/215271935-4dce7b8f-4dbb-4623-b8a2-51dad20a3307.png)\r\n\r\nAnd this is with `winblend = 100`:\r\n\r\n![map_winblend-100](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/24854248/215271948-bd187c17-1c3b-4e9d-9036-78ce1f552eda.png)\r\n\r\nI am not sure why you experience this. Assuming no mixup with actual behavior, probably you have your `hi MiniMapNormal` highlight group with `guibg=NONE`. Together with transparent terminal emulator it makes \"transparent\".",
